{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/943610-how-would-you-limit-condition-abuse-while-staying-mechanically-and-rules-consistant","id":943610,"title":"How would you limit condition abuse while staying mechanically and rules consistant?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-04T07:28:14-07:00","id":943610,"title":"How would you limit condition abuse while staying mechanically and rules consistant?","content":"The second edition changes have made spell casting much more consistent and well defined. However, the heavy use of conditions and the ways that mages now can use conditions are ripe for abuse.<br /> <br /> In what ways would you as the ST reign in condition abuse proactively, while still being consistent in the rules that players can expect to operate under?<br /> <br /> With the ease that mages are able to obtain an exceptional success, conditions are there for the taking.<br /> <br /> The Steadfast condition for example seems to be the most likely abused condition. Mage X casts one of his praxis spells or used Fate to obtain an exceptional success, and thus a favorable condition, on an easy spell with high dice pool. Mage X keeps the Steadfast condition on hand until he wants to cast The Mother Of All Spells. He then increases the potency or introduces other spell dice pool penalties until he has one die left. By resolving the Steadfast condition, the Uber Spell essentially becomes an automatic success.<br /> <br /> But Steadfast is just one condition. Conditions like Inspired and others could just as easily be abused. So I'm thinking that simply doing away with or nerfing the condition itself is not the best answer. Especially given the importance that conditions have in the entire CoD line.<br /> <br /> How about limiting the conditions gained from exceptional spell successes to negative conditions? This would have the benefit of keeping conditions intact and useful, while limiting mage abuse. It would also reinforce, in my mind, the idea that even when spells go right, there is still a price to be paid for the power.<br /> <br /> How would you slow down the condition based beat/bonus gravy train while staying consistent in rules (RAW or house) application?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10978-azenogoth","name":"Azenogoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10978_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T07:37:37-07:00","id":943614,"title":"","content":"The way I read the condition? Steadfast is tied to a specific skill. It won't work unless you're using an appropriate rote. It most certainly won't work with improvised magic. Same with Inspired, same with Informed, same with Shaken. I'd need examples from the third category you mention.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>SHAKEN</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Something has frightened your character extensively. Any<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">time your character is taking an action where that fear might<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">hinder her, you may opt to fail the roll (before you\u2019ve made<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">the roll), and shed this Condition. This Condition can be<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">imposed by a successful degeneration roll.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Example Skills</b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">: Brawl, Firearms, Intimidation, Weaponry</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><b>Resolution: </b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Fail a roll, as noted.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Steadfast only works if you fail a roll. If you are at a chance-die, you just roll a die. It's not automatic successes on demand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 08-04-2016, 10:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T08:01:15-07:00","id":943623,"title":"","content":"Well, I house ruled all GMC Conditions only work for mundane actions unless it was bestowed by Fate with the +2 reach for it to &quot;apply to spellcasting rolls.&quot;<br /> <br /> Aside from that, the RAW is not really clear whether Conditions added in core CofD apply to all types of supernatural actions or not. So, technically there is no RAW to support that it helps supernatural actions and no RAW that states it does not support those actions.<br /> <br /> Now, the Conditions written specifically for Mage indicate whether they apply to spellcasting rolls which leads me to believe that through reading between the lines normal Conditions should not apply to spellcasting or supernatural actions. However, an exceptional success from spellcasting can grant Steadfast, and others as you mentioned so it seems kind of odd to gain a Condition from doing a supernatural action that would not apply to supernatural actions.<br /> <br /> My house rule was made at least in my opinion because as you mentioned &quot;The Mother of All Spells&quot; only needs 1 success to effectively work unlike mundane actions that have varying degrees of success, thus for &quot;Sleepers/Normal Folk&quot; to abuse Steadfast is not that big of a deal honestly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":". 08-04-2016, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T13:38:03-07:00","id":943829,"title":"","content":"Most mundane actions only require one success too though, that's why they built spells to work like that, so that it works similarly to the regular action system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T14:27:56-07:00","id":943877,"title":"","content":"Very true good sir. I just think the power a Mage can wield with one success is just a little too powerful compared to what a Vanilla Mortal/Sleeper could handle with one success. However, it does bring up a good question of how Vampires and Werewolves would treat these as well, since I don't think they have any new conditions that would boost them or aid them in some fashion. *shrugs* So, its kind of a by logic that RAW implicitly states they apply across the board.<br /> <br /> In my opinion, Mages have a perfect alternative that is not too hard to come by if they really want that Steadfast condition to work on their spellcasting rolls. It is a minor inconvenience house rule that merely cuts down on the Praxis - Steadfast - Kill the opponent with Potency 15 spell next round.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":4720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","user":"Taldorblackfire","date":". 08-04-2016, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T15:35:32-07:00","id":943940,"title":"","content":"I don't know about werewolves, but vampires at least have &quot;beneficial&quot; Conditions. They just tend to inflict them on others. I'm not really weighing in with an opinion here btw, other than I don't really have a problem with the rules as written so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T18:05:43-07:00","id":944030,"title":"","content":"I would think that the CoD core book was written to be splat agnostic. Meaning it pertains to all characters in the CoD, not just the mundanes. I do not think that the conditions and tilts in the core book exclude the splats and their abilities just because they do not specifically mention spells, disciplines, contracts, spirit powers, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10978-azenogoth","name":"Azenogoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10978_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T13:09:17-07:00","id":944486,"title":"","content":"As far as Steadfast goes, you still need one die to roll, so at most a +5 bonus from Steadfast, and you need the +2 Reach option. Like Mrmdubois, I too am fine with the rules as set so far.<br /> <br /> As far as your idea of negatives goes, I would definetly not have negative effects for exceptional successes. Exceptional successes are cool things that are to be rewarded. With nice and good Conditions, or other nice and good things from the exceptional success list. Rather than mages being exhillarated at how skillfully or powerfully they've performed, you'd have them almost fear that feeling.<br /> <br /> Ignoring my being fine with the rules for the moment, if you're really worried about Condition abuse and feel asking your players to not be spammy is not a valid way to go for your table, an option is to limit it to a Condition being usable/acquirable only once per scene. You're Steadfast, and you do great from that, but you won't get the same thing from being Steadfast again for a while. Other options for the exceptional success are still viable, as well as allowing the option of gaining an arcane beat directly instead of the Condition. This way they can still get some cool moments from Steadfast, but not always and repeatedly.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T14:11:15-07:00","id":944515,"title":"","content":"I generally wait to see a problem before I try to hack it, but from mild to extreme measures...<br /> <br /> 1) Use Group Beats. This way there's no way that anyone has an XP advantage, so the actual issue is one of pacing.<br /> 2) Enforce the rule that XP expenditure requires that you can justify it through play. You can have all the XP you want, but it can only be used in ways that make sense.<br /> 3) Strongly suggest that they start spending their XP on things that don't blatantly benefit them, such as pursuing a Wisdom dot or increasing Willpower.<br /> 4) Start using time skips. Amorphous time periods make it so that you can reset certain things pretty easily.<br /> 5) And the actual house rule: set a cap on how many XPs you can gain per session/chapter. Doesn't matter how much gravy your train has: it gets truncated after a point.<br /> 6) Walk away. At some point, it isn't worth playing with people who feel a need to do this kind of metagaming because they're not helping you tell a story anymore: they're just having fun tinkering with mechanics. And as long as you're okay with that, then it's okay, but when you're not, then you need to own your discomfort.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, like Aeryes said, the actual solution is to <i>talk to your players</i> and explain that this isn't the kind of game you want to run. As a general rule, I don't play RPGs with people who can't have that kind of conversation and who aren't willing to make a good-faith effort to tell the same kind of story you're going for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T14:37:17-07:00","id":944521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/943610-how-would-you-limit-condition-abuse-while-staying-mechanically-and-rules-consistant?p=943614#post943614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I read the condition? Steadfast is tied to a specific skill. It won't work unless you're using an appropriate rote. It most certainly won't work with improvised magic. Same with Inspired, same with Informed, same with Shaken. I'd need examples from the third category you mention.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I read it, it wouldn't even work if you cast the spell as a Rote and used the appropriate Skill as a Mudra Yantra, because it's still not actually a Skill roll. It's a Gnosis + Arcanum roll with an <i>equipment bonus</i> that happens to be equal to your dots in the Skill. That's what Yantras are, they're spellcasting-specific equipment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T15:06:09-07:00","id":944546,"title":"","content":"Steadfast doesn't care about it being a skill or not. Steadfast is a very weird condition that doesn't have a skill listed for it's procurement. It's one of only Conditions in the game that had <i>no replicable way of being created </i>- without &quot;example skill&quot; and mechanics that specifically called for this Condition, it was very much under GM's control; there was literally no setup that &quot;entitled you&quot; to it. <br /> Which makes sense, because Steadfast is a Condition that simply says &quot;if you failed, you didn't&quot; - basically, it turns 30% odds into 100% odds. It doesn't specify <i>what kind of a roll </i>it affects; it's a &quot;heroic moment on demand&quot; Condition that could be only created by GM's initiative. <br /> The problem here is that with a Rote, you can use Exceptional Luck to grab Steadfast every turn at no cost - you need only one potency to make it work, you need only one turn duration for it to work, and so on. Hell, you don't need a Rote for it - if you have Fate 3, you get 2 reaches on it anyway, which allows you to cast this Reflexively at no Paradox cost to make every action of yours Steadfasted...and if you aren't using it with a Rote, you might as well put a Praxis on it. Because you don't need any Factors on it, you will roll a bucket of dice on it, so Exceptional Successes ahoy. <br /> <br /> If you are using a Rote on it, instead of Praxis, you can apply above to magical rolls. Steadfast isn't &quot;worth +5&quot;; it's really hard to put a numerical value on a ability that allows you to auto succeed as long as you get to roll 1 dice. <br /> It turns Acanthus into Sakamoto from Sakamoto Desu Ga. <br /> Again, this isn't a &quot;white room&quot;. It's my experience of playing an Acanthus with Fate primary that made me loathe choice of my Arcana and if I didn't like my character, I would just scrap the character and ask for something different. <br /> <br /> Errorl's suggestions are good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T15:32:01-07:00","id":944564,"title":"","content":"The problem here is not the condition itself, it's that the condition is underpriced. These conditions are worth around a +3 or +5 dice bonus, but they only cost the Potency of a +1 dice bonus. Therefore, I would say to make it so that spells which apply conditions require 3 to 5 Potency per condition applied.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately however, not all conditions are created equal. Other conditions are worth only a +2 dice bonus, which means you'd need to come up with a table of costs for each condition, which complicates things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 08-05-2016, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T15:36:32-07:00","id":944566,"title":"","content":"I just throw out the Steadfast/Informed and asked my GM to just come up with interesting Luck Conditions created using the (pretty good!) section on creating conditions and tilts in the storytelling section. It's a very good section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T14:30:56-07:00","id":945064,"title":"","content":"Bottom-line? Attach Steadfast to skills like I suggest, same way all the other relevant conditions work. That pretty much covers all the possible abuse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T21:23:24-07:00","id":945273,"title":"","content":"I have actually done that. Created luck conditions I mean. There's three, each with a different twist that changes when and how you would apply it and they can all either be good or bad (so can be used to curse or bless, whichever fits)<br /> <br /> Of course the player with Fate... never actually showed up for the third session and hasn't since, so the point became moot <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Personally I rather like the conditions though. They were fun to both make and use In Game (NPCs)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T01:33:42-07:00","id":945358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asaram</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/943610-how-would-you-limit-condition-abuse-while-staying-mechanically-and-rules-consistant?p=945273#post945273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have actually done that. Created luck conditions I mean. There's three, each with a different twist that changes when and how you would apply it and they can all either be good or bad (so can be used to curse or bless, whichever fits)<br /> <br /> Of course the player with Fate... never actually showed up for the third session and hasn't since, so the point became moot <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Personally I rather like the conditions though. They were fun to both make and use In Game (NPCs)</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not post them? I'm always interested in more custom conditions. There was a thread on them over in the main CoD part of the forum (back when it was still GMC), but it has sadly sunk down since then. Could post them here, or perhaps better to revive this thread: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/144034-fan-made-conditions\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ade-conditions</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}